# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 11 of the Tutorial

[A low-pass RC (the Bode plot)]

e,1,0,1
r1,1,2,1000
c1,2,0,1e-6

analysis: ac
omega: 1
note: The Plot card re-solves the circuit at every frequency, which is why it takes the circuit and an answer's name rather than an expression.
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
plottool: bode
plotkey: v_2
plotmin: 10
plotmax: 100000
plotpoints: 300


[AS7's Example 14.7 (series resonance)]

e,1,0,20
r,1,2,2
l,2,3,1'm
c,3,0,.4'u

analysis: ac
omega: w
note: For the bandwidth frequencies, solve abs(ze) = sqrt(2)*2 with w<50000 and then w>50000: 49010 and 51010 rad/s.
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
solve_equations: im(ze) = 0
solve_unknowns: w
solve_conditions: w>0
solve_real_only: yes


[AS7's Example 14.8 (parallel resonance)]

e,1,0,10
r,1,0,8'k
l,1,0,.2'm
c,1,0,8'u

analysis: ac
omega: w
note: The chapter uses im(ie) rather than im(ze) here because the calculator's numerical search could not find so sharp a peak. Version 9 solves symbolically and would manage either, but the equation says something true: at resonance the source's current is in phase with its voltage.
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
solve_equations: im(ie) = 0
solve_unknowns: w
solve_conditions: w>0
solve_real_only: yes


[AS7's Example 14.9 (resonance from a node voltage)]

j,0,1,1
c,1,0,.1
r1,1,0,10
l,1,2,2
r2,2,0,2

analysis: ac
omega: w
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
solve_equations: im(v1) = 0
solve_unknowns: w
solve_conditions: w>0
solve_real_only: yes
